00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:25.320
And particularly lucrative,

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:26.610
because of the premium price

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:28.830
that good extra virgin olive oil commands.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:32.130
Because of this Italy has
an entire investigative unit

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:33.930
dedicated to food fraud,

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:36.510
and they're regularly
busting these fraud schemes.

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:37.650
Some of them are less extreme

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.030
than the ones we've talked about.

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:41.670
A really common one is people will ship in

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:44.970
olive oil from Spain, they
will bottle it in Italy

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:46.500
and then they will put a label

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:48.630
that says that it's Italian olive oil

00:12:48.630 --> 00:12:50.130
and they will sell it at a higher premium

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:53.010
because Italian olive oil
commands a higher price.

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:54.930
But oftentimes it's even
more subtle than that.

00:12:54.930 --> 00:12:58.200
Olive oil companies will
mix extra virgin olive oil

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:01.538
with old or decaying oil
or they'll use olives

00:13:01.538 --> 00:13:04.290
that have been sitting
on the floor of the grove

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:05.550
for like a couple of weeks

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:07.800
and they're like, eh, we will
just like press them anyway

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:09.246
and call it extra virgin olive oil.

00:13:09.246 --> 00:13:11.400
And it's not, it's a different thing.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:13.710
Again, this is a really
complex supply chain

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:16.800
with lots of opportunities
for people to step in

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:19.320
and change it from this delicate liquid

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:21.990
called extra virgin olive
oil to something else,

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:23.670
and it's really hard to detect.

00:13:23.670 --> 00:13:27.540
A lot of this olive oil ends
up on your supermarket shelf

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:30.210
with a photo of a humble Italian farmer

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:33.930
in an idyllic landscape
with words like cold pressed

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:37.950
or premium selection with
pretend stamps of approval

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:39.510
that don't mean anything.

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:40.343
I mean listen,

00:13:40.343 --> 00:13:42.870
these could all be legit
extra virgin olive oils

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:45.660
but I don't know because here in the US

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:48.270
we actually have no enforcement standards.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.403
Luckily scientists have tested this.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:53.400
One of the first big tests on this

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:57.390
was from researchers at UC
Davis, a college in California.

00:13:57.390 --> 00:13:59.310
They went out and bought
a bunch of olive oil

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:01.230
from stores in California.

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:03.900
They tested them to see
if they met the standards

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:08.040
for extra virgin olive oil
and they found that 69%

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.600
of imported olive oil

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:11.880
that was claiming to be extra virgin

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:14.250
failed to meet the
internationally recognized

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:16.770
sensory standards where
an expert tastes it

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:19.500
and can tell if it's
actually extra virgin or not.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:23.940
And of those 31% failed to
meet the chemical standards,

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:25.350
meaning they were too acidic.

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:28.470
A lot of this stuff is not
extra virgin olive oil.

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:29.820
Now I'm sure I'm gonna get an email

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:31.500
from people in the olive oil industry

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:34.110
saying that this study
isn't actually legit

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:35.744
because it was only a sample size

00:14:35.744 --> 00:14:38.490
of olive oil in stores in California.

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:41.010
But this was actually just
one of several studies

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:43.260
over the years that have
shown the same thing.

00:14:43.260 --> 00:14:45.960
Most of the olive oil on our shelves

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:48.540
claiming to be that amazing golden liquid

00:14:48.540 --> 00:14:50.850
that is delicately produced and stored

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:52.800
and contains the fullness of the taste

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:54.840
and the health benefits of olives,

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:56.550
AKA extra virgin olive oil,

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:59.160
most of these labels are lying.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:02.790
Now most of the oil in these
bottles does come from olives.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:04.620
Like there's not a lot of that fraud

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:05.850
where they're like taking seed oil

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:07.020
and pretending that it's olive oil

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:08.280
that's been clamped down on.

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:09.690
Still happens, but not very often.

00:15:09.690 --> 00:15:11.610
But again, it being made from olives

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:14.400
is not what makes extra
virgin olive oil special.

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:15.750
It is the way that it's made.

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:16.950
It's the way that it's processed.

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:20.040
It's how quickly they take
the fruit from the grove

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:23.370
and they press it and bottle
it and store it and ship it.

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:24.950
This oil is not that.

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.240
It is not extra virgin anymore.

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:29.280
And yet they slap a
label so that you and I

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:31.110
feel like we're getting the best stuff

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:32.670
and we're getting it for a good price.

00:15:32.670 --> 00:15:34.860
You would be in big
trouble if you got caught

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:36.900
labeling it as such in Italy

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:38.670
and a lot of European countries.

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:40.470
But wait, why haven't these companies

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:43.890
who are doing it in the United
States gotten in trouble?

00:15:43.890 --> 00:15:47.010
Because in America we don't care.

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:50.580
Whereas in Italy they literally
have laws that are violated

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:52.980
when you label something
as extra virgin olive oil

00:15:52.980 --> 00:15:53.813
and it's not.

00:15:53.813 --> 00:15:55.740
Here in the US, we have no laws for this.

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:57.960
Companies don't have
to test their olive oil

00:15:57.960 --> 00:15:59.880
to prove that it's extra virgin.

00:15:59.880 --> 00:16:01.110
They can just import them

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:03.510
and slap on extra virgin to the label

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:05.370
and no one can do anything about it.

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:08.190
Between this and the
fact that most Americans

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:09.023
probably don't know

00:16:09.023 --> 00:16:11.010
what extra virgin olive
oil even takes like

00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:12.870
so they don't know what to expect.

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:15.750
The US has become what one expert calls

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:18.030
the dumping grounds for olive oil

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:20.433
that says it's extra virgin and it's not.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:24.360
So is there any hope here?

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:26.610
Can you ever try the real stuff

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:31.610
extra virgin olive oil that
is like magical golden liquid?

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:33.510
Yes you can.

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:34.800
It exists.

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.780
You just need to know what to look for.

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:39.690
We put together a list of tips

00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:42.060
on how you can find legitimate
extra virgins olive oil

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.130
and know that you're
getting the good stuff.

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:45.750
I'm gonna put the link in the description.

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:46.890
It's everything from the material

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:48.330
that the bottle is made out of

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:51.690
to the nuances in the
packaging and labeling

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:54.840
and the date labeling, the quality seals.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:57.660
We also give you some ideas
on some of the trickery

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.970
that companies try to fake it

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:02.400
to try to make it look
legit but it's actually not.

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:04.050
So that link is in a description.

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:06.120
If you want to try extra virgin olive oil

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:08.190
and get your hands on it and
are willing to pay for it

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:10.650
because spoiler alert it is more expensive

00:17:10.650 --> 00:17:12.750
than the fake stuff that's
pretending to be real,

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:14.070
then you can go check out that doc

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:15.510
and hopefully it's helpful.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:17.970
The point is that it is possible

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:19.920
and I guess if you're still
here watching this video

00:17:19.920 --> 00:17:22.890
you're wondering why is this so important?

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:26.940
Like why are we talking about
oil and olive oil fraud?

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:28.170
And there are a couple answers.

00:17:28.170 --> 00:17:32.400
Number one is that this is a
really amazing old tradition.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:34.770
It's a tradition that
fueled the civilizations

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:37.620
in the Mediterranean
for thousands of years.

00:17:37.620 --> 00:17:40.830
The harvesting and pressing
and bottling and consumption

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:45.450
of olive oil, good olive oil
is an old delicate tradition.

00:17:45.450 --> 00:17:47.700
And when you mix capitalism with that

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:49.440
you often get a race to the the bottom

00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:52.500
on who can make it the cheapest
and sell it for the cheapest

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.000
so that they can make the most money.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:55.110
And inevitably you will get

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:58.260
opportunistic people who try to trick you

00:17:58.260 --> 00:17:59.940
to make you think that it's the real thing

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:00.990
so that you'll pay for it.

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:02.670
And this hurts the producers

00:18:02.670 --> 00:18:05.610
who are actually doing the
resource intensive process

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:08.220
of harvesting and processing
this in the right way.

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:11.910
And at the end of the day, to
me, it is absolutely worth it.

00:18:11.910 --> 00:18:15.780
Good extra virgin olive oil
is unlike anything else.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:16.890
A few years ago I discovered

00:18:16.890 --> 00:18:19.500
that I had never actually
tasted extra virgin olive oil.

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:21.330
So I bought my first bottle.

00:18:21.330 --> 00:18:24.270
It was kind of expensive, it was like $25

00:18:24.270 --> 00:18:26.340
and I started using it on everything.

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:29.730
I even started drinking it raw
just to like get the flavor

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:31.710
because I'm kind of weird
and that's what I do

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:34.320
and I'm sorry, but it's just delicious.

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:39.150
And I started to understand
why this stuff became so sacred

00:18:39.150 --> 00:18:41.280
for so many cultures in the Mediterranean.

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:44.550
Why it's like a part of
every major religion.

00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:48.180
Why it has endured as a
health and culinary staple.

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:50.850
And I guess in knowing how
valuable this liquid is

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:53.190
I actually understand why fraudsters

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:55.470
and the mafia got involved here,

00:18:55.470 --> 00:18:57.480
why they tried to deceive us

00:18:57.480 --> 00:18:59.580
into thinking that we are consuming

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:03.114
the most magical liquid on
earth, even if we're not.

